<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34986" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-fūsĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a pouring over</i> or <i>upon</i>,
				<i>a wetting</i>, <i>moistening</i>
			(post-Aug.). perfusio corporis ex aquā calidā,
				<i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 7, 14, §
			74</span></i>.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alarum perfusiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 9, 82, § 164</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>baptism</i>, <i><span class="en">Lact. 4,
				15, 1</span></i>.</div>
